d the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/52/523dccf73169d02b6bdf4297e96ec84bcc6c43213cdd722000f3a987a534b218.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n$$\nc_2 e^{-2t} {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}t \\\\ - t + 1\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$\nWhen $c_2=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=t{e}^{-2t} \\\\ y &=(-t+1){e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$t$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-0.5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1.36$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.18$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4.08$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.18$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/db/dbf5a13ecd5e81c399204fd29d235e410fcb62274555cf3e5b32a383c1078d24.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/6c/6c84cd04f3b037bee48d02d3183114e2668fbbd110bd44e9311e7ff454db8bac.png)" 13194139544863 17592186576411 false] [17592186166546 1074 "Since we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda=-2$ (of multiplicity two) and only one corresponding eigenvector $\\mathbf{v},$ the solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = c_1\\mathbf{v} e^{\\lambda t}  + c_2 (\\mathbf{v}  te^{\\lambda t}  +  \\mathbf{w}e^{\\lambda t} \\, ),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{w}$ i